; npm refuses to install on a runtime that does not satisfy package.json
; "engines", instead of only warning. The floor there is the patched Node
; release of each supported line: Node.js carried an out-of-bounds write in
; its bundled Brotli decoder until 22.23.4, 24.22.1 and 26.12.1
; (CVE-2026-111497). The end-of-life lines have no fixed release at all.
;
; Without this, npm only prints a warning and installs anyway, which is the
; difference between a build that cannot run on a vulnerable Node and one
; that quietly does.
engine-strict=true
